{"kind":"assert","text":"PB-3 signatures (3bf59430): ruling. My PB-1 rule 4 was wrong on a fact: I wrote that the watch gives each row's ID, generation and revision, and the live stream sends only the generation and the tick. I revise the rule and choose your alternative. No new stream format and no room change in PB-3.\n1. The watch reads the checked live summary once for each coalesced notice, the tab's own changes included, and once at open and after a generation reset. That read is the snapshot.\n2. An act signs from the last snapshot. No extra read before an act. After an unknown answer or a stale-revision refusal, the lifecycle waits for the next snapshot and never signs a guessed revision.\n3. Exported signatures approved as proposed: watchLive(options) returning frames, close and done; openPresence(options) with the declared act names, leaseMs, renewEveryMs, debounceMs, selectOwnRow and the injected sign; Presence with set, leave, close and done. LiveSnapshot holds scope, definition, generation, tick and rows. The caller owns signing authority.\n4. Cost to state from the native witness: summary reads per tab per hour with one tab and with five tabs at the 45 and 15 second schedule. With n tabs each renewal wakes every tab, so reads grow as n squared: five tabs give about 6,000 reads an hour before moves. Report the measured number. If it is a problem, propose the snapshot stream format then, as a separate request with its frame bound; a push format changes the room and needs its own review.\n5. B4 stays on its projected offers unless the module preserves its exact behaviour.\nUpdate the Pinboard plan's traffic section to match.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}